    "created_at": "2022-05-09T12:32:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-09T12:32:24Z",
    "body": "It looks like for now we should fix the obvious security hole and add something like the fish patch (though it would be nice not to break the built-in fsmonitor). This may have to be expanded further into an allow-list for repositories.\r\nWith an allow-list, we should probably opt into opening untrusted repositories in libgit2 and only disable git-cli powered modules, as things like the `git_branch` module should be safe to extract from not explicitly trusted repositories. That said, libgit2 likely still has some security holes (git-lfs style hooks?).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
